# SYNOPSIS

```text
userboot.next=bin/launcher launcher.until=sd-test
```

# DESCRIPTION

sd-test is the last service of the SD image, `bootfs-sdhci-test.img`, which holds devmgr(8) with its drivers and the services its manifest mounts.
The boot-sdhci test boots it in QEMU with an SD card and an eMMC, each in a version 3 sdhci-pci host (`tools/qemu.sh --sd` and `--emmc`), each 64 MiB, made by vx-disk(1) with a taisce partition, anew each run.
The launcher runs until sd-test ends and exits with its code (launcher(8)).

It waits up to 30 seconds for each sdhci(3) to bring its device up or fail, and prints each driver's `status`, a line each, `sd-test: <service>: <line>`.
It checks that each came up, that one is an SD card and one an eMMC, and that devmgr binds two disks at `/dev/sdM*`.
For each disk it checks that its `ctl` answers with the disk's geometry and its `taisce` partition, read from its GPT, and prints that `ctl`; then it writes 160 KiB of random bytes to its `data` 64 KiB in, past the partition table, so the driver takes two pieces of its 128 KiB buffer, and checks that they read back the same, and that 100 bytes read at an offset no sector starts at are the bytes written there.
A line for each check is `sd-test: ok:` or `sd-test: FAILED:` and what it checks; its last line is `sd-test: passed` or `sd-test: <n> failed`.
It exits 0 if every check passed.

# FILES

: `build/<arch>/esp-sdhci-test`
